# Keep the container build context to exactly what container/Dockerfile
# COPYs (core/go.mod, core/go.sum, core/cmd/, core/internal/,
# core/migrations/) plus whatever Docker itself needs to see this file.
# Everything else here would either bloat the context for no reason or
# actively undermine reproducibility: the Dockerfile passes -buildvcs=false
# precisely because the build isn't supposed to depend on .git being
# present or clean, so .git is excluded rather than merely ignored by that
# flag.
.git
.github
.claude

# Not needed by the build; excluding them keeps an in-progress edit to one
# of these from invalidating Docker's layer cache for no reason.
docs
container
README.md
*.md

# Test fixtures and their scratch output; never part of the shipped binary.
# core/tests, not tests: the root tests/ moved under core/ with #106/B1.1,
# and the un-prefixed pattern is dead today (the current Dockerfile never
# COPYs anything that would match it) but would silently stop excluding
# anything the day a future COPY core/ ... starts matching it instead.
core/tests

# Never let a filled-in .env reach the build context.
.env
container/.env
